<% layout('layouts/homepageLayout') %>
<div class="container my-5">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="text-muted">Last updated: October 30, 2026</p>

  <p>CSMM (Catalysm's Server Manager) is a management tool for 7 Days to Die game servers. This page explains what data
    CSMM collects, why, and what you can do about it.</p>

  <h3>Data we collect</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account data:</strong> when you log in with Steam or Discord we store your Steam ID, Discord user ID,
      username and avatar, so we can link your account to the servers and players you manage or play on.</li>
    <li><strong>Game server data:</strong> for servers connected to CSMM we store data reported by the game server, such
      as player names, game IDs, IP address and country, in-game position, inventory, playtime and statistics. This is
      needed for features like player management, bans, the economy and player tracking.</li>
    <li><strong>Discord data:</strong> when a server admin adds the CSMM bot to their Discord server, we store the IDs
      of the guild, channels and roles the admin configures. Message content is only read in channels the admin has set
      up (for example the chat bridge) and is relayed to the game server; it is not stored.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> application logs and basic usage statistics, used to keep the service running
      and to fix problems.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>How we use data</h3>
  <p>Data is only used to provide CSMM's features to server owners and their players. We do not sell data and do not
    use it for advertising or to train AI models.</p>

  <h3>Sharing</h3>
  <p>Server owners and admins who use CSMM can see the data of players on their servers. Bans that server owners add
    to the global ban list are visible to other CSMM users. We use Steam and Discord to log you in, and Cookiebot to
    manage cookie consent. Other than that, data is not shared with third parties, except the hosting and
    infrastructure providers that run CSMM.</p>

  <h3>Retention</h3>
  <p>Tracking data (such as location and inventory history) is kept for a limited time and deleted automatically.
    Other data is kept as long as the related account or server is active in CSMM.</p>

  <h3>Cookies</h3>
  <p>CSMM uses cookies to keep you logged in. Cookie consent is managed through Cookiebot.</p>

  <h3>Your rights</h3>
  <p>You can ask us to see, correct or delete your data. Server owners can delete a server from CSMM at any time,
    which removes the data related to it.</p>

  <h3>Contact</h3>
  <p>For privacy questions or data requests, open an issue on
    <a href="https://github.com/CatalysmsServerManager/7-days-to-die-server-manager/issues" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
    or reach out through the support channels listed on <a href="https://docs.csmm.app" target="_blank">docs.csmm.app</a>.</p>

  <h3>Cookie declaration</h3>
  <script id="CookieDeclaration" src="https://consent.cookiebot.com/4408463b-a496-4521-a276-ed6540d2d52f/cd.js"
    type="text/javascript" async></script>
</div>
